                    How can a robot move safely around an interventional imaging system without blocking the anatomy clinicians need to see?
                  </p>
                </div>
                <div class="zm-point">
                  <strong data-en="My contribution" data-zh="我的工作">My contribution</strong>
                  <p
                    data-en="I am integrating the patient-side scene model with MoveIt, updating the robot and Loop-X poses, and developing geometry-based trajectory selection that considers collisions, singularity risk, motion efficiency, and target occlusion."
                    data-zh="我正在将患者侧操作场景模型接入 MoveIt，更新机器人与 Loop-X 的位姿，并根据 X 射线源、探测器和目标区域之间的几何关系筛选轨迹，同时考虑碰撞、奇异位形、运动效率和成像遮挡。"
                  >
                    I am integrating the patient-side scene model with MoveIt, updating the robot and Loop-X poses, and developing geometry-based
                    trajectory selection that considers collisions, singularity risk, motion efficiency, and target occlusion.
                  </p>
